      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 12 - EGX Daily Master Workflow\n\nOrchestrates the full daily pipeline in order: universe -> daily update -> (trading-day gate) -> technical analysis -> support/resistance -> volume analysis -> breakout/momentum/pullback/reversal scanners -> overall ranking -> report.\n\nRuns on a schedule (default 21:00 Africa/Cairo, Sun-Thu — EGX's trading week) or on demand via the Manual Trigger ('Run EGX Scanner Now', spec section 35). Pushed later than the ~14:30 close because EODHD's EGX EOD publish time lags and varies (confirmed via live testing: not yet published even at 17:00) — 03's own retry schedule (16:00-20:30, every 30 min) is what actually catches the data as soon as it's live; 21:00 gives that window time to close before the full scan runs.\n\n**Note on scheduling:** n8n's Schedule Trigger cron expression is evaluated at workflow-registration time, not per-execution, so it can't read DAILY_SCAN_HOUR/DAILY_SCAN_MINUTE at runtime. If you change those env vars, also edit the Schedule Trigger node's cron expression to match.\n\n**Before first use:** open every Execute Workflow node below and reselect the target sub-workflow from the dropdown — n8n assigns new workflow IDs on import, so these references start unset (see docs/IMPORT-N8N.md).",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "c9f7982a-f623-4616-98c3-122cc85e6be6"
    },
